    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nModeline support landed with #30257 only accepts modelines if they *strictly* stand at the beginning of query string, lexically speaking.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nvim.print(vim.treesitter.query.get(lang, \"highlights\")) -- Full of native stuff.\nlocal q = [[;query\n  ;; extends\n  ((identifier) @variable.builtin (#set! priority 200))\n]]\nvim.treesitter.query.set(\"lua\", \"highlights\", q) -- Not \"extended\" I think, because..\nvim.print(vim.treesitter.query.get(lang, \"highlights\")) -- .. only my pattern remains.\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI would expect the `;; extend` modeline to be respected in the above and the `highlights` query not to be cleared, even though an additional `; query` comment is standing above it.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1321+gb169d9376c Build type: RelWithDebInfo LuaJIT 2.1.1785763465\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\ndoesn't apply?\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux etak 7.1.8-arch1-3 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:16:08 +0000 x86_64 GNU/Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm 20240203-110809-5046fc22\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nchaotic-AUR `neovim-nightly-bin`",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
